Here, `_size` is the count of the items in the ArrayList before the `Add` method is called and `RET` is the return value of the `Add` method. The assertion is checking that the count of the ArrayList (which is `_size`) increases by 1 when an element is added to the ArrayList. Please note that this only works if the `Add` method is called and does not throw an exception, as the assertion can't handle such situations. Also, due to the nature of software testing, it's difficult to check the entire list in a single assertion. This assertion is checking only at the end of the execution of the Add method.
